   "text": "This is a brew. No storm deck shows up in the current Premodern field. Only one Scourge storm card is both green and legal here: Hunting Pack. The others I checked are either illegal or off-color. Tendrils of Agony, Grapeshot and Mind's Desire are illegal in Premodern. Brain Freeze, Temporal Fissure and Wing Shards are legal but not green. So I built on the Elves shell and made Hunting Pack the finisher.\n\n**What the field data says**\n- Elves has 3 appearances in the field list, 0.6% of the meta. The card stats cover 7 Elves decks. One of them runs 2 Hunting Pack (14%). It has shown up in 31 lists across the format.\n- Gabaman went 5-0 in a League on 10/11 with this core: Survival, Cradle, Priest, Quirion Ranger, Multani's Acolyte and Wirewood Symbiote.\n\n**How the storm count builds**\n- **Free and cheap spells:** Llanowar Elves, Fyndhorn Elves, Quirion Ranger and Wirewood Symbiote each cost one mana. Lotus Petal costs zero. Every cast adds to the storm count.\n- **Replaying creatures:** Multani's Acolyte and Wirewood Symbiote return elves to your hand so you can cast them again for more storm.\n- **Mana:** Gaea's Cradle (in 100% of Elves lists) and Priest of Titania (100%) produce the big mana for Hunting Pack. Hunting Pack is an instant, so you can also cast it at the end of the opponent's turn.\n- **Payoff:** With storm at 6, one Hunting Pack makes seven 4/4s.\n- **Wirewood Lodge:** It untaps a Priest or adds another use of an elf. It has not shown up in recent results.\n\n**What I changed from stock Elves**\n- I cut the red splash. That means no Anger, Squee or Mountain. Survival still finds Deranged Hermit, Yavimaya Granger and Masticore.\n- I cut Tangle Wire (43% of lists). In its place are 4 Lotus Petal and 4 Hunting Pack.\n\n**Sideboard**\n- It follows the usual Elves board: Naturalize (100%), Tormod's Crypt (71%), Xantid Swarm and Uktabi Orangutan.\n- Winter Orb (57% of Elves boards) works against your own mana. Only bring it in if you're the one doing the locking.\n\n**Risks**\n- Hunting Pack costs 7. A slow hand of mana creatures loses to Sligh (10.6% of the meta) and to sweepers.\n- Tune it in Leagues before you take it to a Challenge.",
