   "id": "premodern-replenish-twist",
   "format": "Premodern",
   "sentFormat": "Premodern",
   "prompt": "Build a Replenish deck in Premodern that doesn't play blue.",
   "status": 200,
   "ms": 43894,
   "text": "I built a Green-White (GW) Replenish deck for Premodern. It plays no blue. It passed the format check with no errors.\n\n**Why green-white.** Every one of the 37 Replenish lists in the last 30 days plays blue. Attunement, Frantic Search, Intuition and Island are in all or nearly all of them. You can't get the stock list without blue. The closest real non-blue shell is Enchantress. It's tier A at 13.8% of the field, and 95 of its 96 lists run Replenish. So I took that shell and moved it toward the Replenish combo.\n\n**Combo pieces.**\n- 3 Replenish. Enchantress lists average 2.2. I went up one so you see it more often.\n- 4 Parallax Wave and 3 Opalescence. Enchantress lists average 2.7 and 2.6. With Opalescence out, Parallax Wave turns into a creature and can exile itself.\n\n**Getting enchantments into the graveyard.** Without blue you lose Attunement and Frantic Search. The deck fills the graveyard these ways instead:\n- Seal of Cleansing (3) and Aura of Silence (1) sacrifice themselves.\n- Solitary Confinement (2) makes you discard a card every upkeep.\n- The rest comes from opponents removing your enchantments.\n\n**Engine.** 4 Argothian Enchantress, 4 Enchantress's Presence, 4 Wild Growth, 3 Sterling Grove and 3 Mirri's Guile. Mirri's Guile is at 3, down from the usual 4, to make room for the extra combo copies.\n\n**Lands.** Brushland, Serra's Sanctum, Windswept Heath, Wooded Foothills, Forest and Plains. No land in the deck makes blue mana.\n\n**Sideboard.** This follows the usual Enchantress board. Xantid Swarm shows up in 97% of those boards, Tormod's Crypt in 98%, Aura of Silence in 82%, Sacred Ground in 81% and Gaea's Blessing in 72%.\n\n**This is a brew.** The list is almost all stock Enchantress cards. But no recorded result runs 3 Replenish and 4 Parallax Wave in this shell, so treat it as untested. For a matchup-specific sideboard plan, name the opponent and I'll check the board against it.",
