   "prompt": "I want a Modern Merfolk deck that can beat the current top decks.",
   "status": 200,
   "ms": 33382,
   "text": "I built mono-blue Merfolk for Modern and it passed the legality check. It copies a real 5-0 Modern League list from Oct 13. The same player went 5-0 with nearly the same 75 on Oct 12. The only change between the two was 3 Subtlety in place of 3 Propaganda in the sideboard.\n\n**Sample size.** Only 6 Merfolk lists showed up in the last 30 days. Both 5-0s came from that one player. I have no matchup win rates, so I can't promise this list beats the top decks. I can only show how the cards line up against them.\n\n**The two top decks**\n- Broodscale Combo is 17.3% of the field.\n- Prowess is 9.3% of the field.\n\n**Main deck**\n- **Harbinger of the Seas** is in 6 of 6 lists. It turns nonbasic lands into Islands, and both top decks rely on nonbasics.\n  - Broodscale plays about 16.7 nonbasics: Eldrazi Temple, Urza's Saga and Ugin's Labyrinth.\n  - Prowess plays about 15.3: Steam Vents and fetchlands.\n- **Aether Vial and Cavern of Souls** are each in 83% of lists. They get your creatures past counterspells.\n- **Flare of Denial and Sink into Stupor** are each in 83% of lists. Snapback is in 50%. These give you free or cheap interaction.\n\n**Sideboard**\nI scored all four cards against both matchups. Every card hit.\n- **4 Chalice of the Void.** Set it to 1 against Prowess, which plays about 4 Dragon's Rage Channeler and 3.8 Monastery Swiftspear. Set it to 2 against Broodscale to stop Basking Broodscale (4 copies) and Haywire Mite.\n- **4 Consign to Memory.** It counters colorless spells, and Broodscale's Eldrazi are colorless: Basking Broodscale, Sowing Mycospawn, Emrakul and Devourer of Destiny. It is in 83% of Merfolk sideboards.\n- **4 Force of Negation.** It counters noncreature spells for free on the opponent's turn. Use it against Prowess spells and combo pieces.\n- **3 Propaganda.** Each attacker costs 2 mana. That slows the 1/1 and 1/2 Prowess creatures and also taxes an Emrakul attack.\n\n**Option:** Use 3 Subtlety instead of Propaganda if you see more Broodscale than Prowess. It puts a creature spell back on top or bottom of the library, such as Devourer of Destiny or Sowing Mycospawn.",
